| tail -20 && ./gradlew test-integration --rerun --tests '*ProviderPaymentIntegrationTest*' -q 2>&1 | tail -20; echo EXIT $?","timeout":600000,"description":"Format, compile, run provider integration tests"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TdgqG4CT3HEdYk5n4YgF3y","tool_input":{"command":"for t in \"test --rerun\" \"test-integration --rerun\" \"test-e2e --rerun\" \"test-architecture\" \"spotlessCheck\"; do ./gradlew $t > /tmp/tidy-out.txt 2>&1 && echo \"$t: passed\" || { echo \"$t: FAILED\"; tail -30 /tmp/tidy-out.txt; }; done","timeout":600000,"description":"Run unit, integration, e2e, architecture, format checks"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":20,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I made one refactoring in the tidy stage for `pay-through-the-provider`, and every check passes. The notes are in `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/tidy.md`.\n\n**The change:** In `RestPaymentProvider.java`, the 20-line block that interprets the provider's reply now sits in its own private method, `translate(response, sessionId)`. That method holds the whole translation of the reply (the anti-corruption layer): `402` means refused, `201` with a reference means success, and anything else means unavailable. It also reads the status code once instead of three times. `initiatePayment` now just builds the request, sends it and translates the answer. Behaviour, messages and log lines are unchanged, and no test was touched.\n\n**Left alone, with the reasons in the file:**\n- **`PaymentResult.failure(..)` naming:** it now means \"refused\", so a name like `refused(..)` would be clearer. The plan says the factory keeps its name, so this is a naming question for the judge stage.\n- **The address setting appears three times:** `checkout.payment-provider.base-url` is written in two activation conditions and in the properties record. I didn't lift it into a constant because that would make the two opposite conditions harder to read side by side.\n- **`SubmitPaymentUseCase` and `PaymentPageController`:** I kept the two `if`s and the two catch blocks as they are. Merging the catch blocks would hide which failure shows which message.\n- **Out-of-date JavaDoc:** the one on `PaymentInitiationFailedException` still says the customer sees the provider's reason. That type is outside this story's changed files, so it's for the document stage.\n\n**Checks:** I ran `testClasses`, `test`, `test-integration` (the provider integration test also ran right after the change), `test-e2e`, `test-architecture` and `spotlessCheck`; all passed. I applied `dca-discipline` to the edited file: the adapter still implements the port, and the provider's wire types stay private to it.","ttft_ms":3085,"type":"result","duration_ms":320354,"uuid":"ea89b6c9-5792-4c8d-b11b-778b1cf8f77c","ttft_stream_ms":1805,"time_to_request_ms":86,"first_content_frame_ms":1806,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
